{title: Frankie and Johnny}
{artist: Traditional American}
{key: C}
{tempo: 100}
{difficulty: beginner}
{tags: folk, blues, americana}
{comment: A twelve-bar blues: four bars of C, two of F, two of C, two of G7, and two back home on C.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Frankie and Johnny were [C]sweethearts
Oh [C]Lordy, how they [C]could love
Swore to be [F]true to each [F]other
Just as [C]true as the [C]stars above
He was [G7]her man, [G7]
But he was [C]doing her [C]wrong

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Frankie went down to the [C]corner
Just for a [C]bucket of [C]beer
She said, [F]"Oh, Mister bar[F]tender
Has my [C]loving Johnny [C]been here?
He's [G7]my man, [G7]
But he's [C]doing me [C]wrong"
